/* ----------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Section G: S6 payload vectors -- ANNOUNCE, HELLO, WELCOME, BYE, PING,
 * PONG, RUMBLE, LED, STATUS, ACK, ERROR (PROTOCOL.md S6.2-S6.11).
 *
 * Every field is a distinctive, non-zero, non-repeating value -- never
 * all-zero, which would pass against a decoder reading the wrong offset.
 * Every named reserved0/reserved1 byte is sent non-zero on the wire and
 * MUST decode as zero (S2 scrub). Type-specific receive-side rules are
 * exercised at their boundaries: S6.2 pairing_required (any non-zero -> 1),
 * S6.3 caps bits 14-31 (masked off), S6.4 key_material (MUST be all-zero
 * on decode AND MUST be forced to zero on encode regardless of input --
 * see apad_welcome_encode_vectors for the encode side), S6.8
 * player_index (>4 -> 0, but 0 itself is untouched).
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

